# Backend Core Architecture Engine

This repository contains the fundamental operational architecture and lower-level algorithmic layers designed for robust backend application frameworks. Written in C++, it highlights clean separation of concerns, algorithmic design patterns, and efficient execution loops necessary for high-throughput transactional processing.

## 🚀 Key Architectural Features
* **High-Throughput Core:** Engineered for computational processing tasks where execution speed and minimal memory footings are strict constraints.
* **Modular Code Structure:** Structured to abstract business logic routines from system IO protocols, mimicking core components found in Automated Banking Systems (ABS).
* **Algorithmic Stability:** Focused on predictable data workflows, thread-safety layouts, and deterministic transaction validation algorithms.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack & Prerequisites
* **Language:** Modern ISO C++
* **Build Configuration:** Standard GCC / Clang toolkit
* **Development Target:** Linux Server Environments (RedHat, Debian, Alpine)

## 🔨 Compilation Guide

You can easily compile the backend core framework using standard terminal tooling:

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com
cd backend-core

# 2. Compile using GCC
g++ -O3 main.cpp -o backend_core_engine

# 3. Launch the engine
./backend_core_engine
```

## 💼 Domain Application
This architecture serves as a blueprint for microservice routing infrastructure, secure transactional processing hubs, and asynchronous server-side computations in the financial technology industry.
